message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Cephalometry Studio: an open-source, browser-based platform for cephalometric analysis and orthodontic research"
authors:
  - family-names: "Nabil Ibrahim Salem Shaesha"
    given-names: "Mohamed"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-7190-1364"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-15
repository-code: "https://github.com/Muhammad-Nabeel-Sh/CephalometryStudio"
url: "https://cephalometry-studio.vercel.app/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - cephalometry
  - orthodontics
  - medical imaging
  - statistics
  - browser
abstract: >-
  Cephalometry Studio is a free, open-source, browser-based application for
  cephalometric analysis. It combines manual and template-assisted landmarking
  (40+ analyses, 500+ landmarks, 23 markup types), calibration-aware
  measurements, a clinical interpretation engine, and seven integrated research
  modules (reliability, descriptive/normative, comparative, longitudinal,
  correlation, diagnostic, and superimposition) with publication-style tables,
  charts, and CSV export. All computation and storage is client-side, so
  patient data never leaves the user's device.
